# `{{module}}` module

Scaffolded with `make new-module name={{module}} feature={{feature}}`. This document is
the **public API contract** for the module: what other modules and the app shell may
import, and how the boundary is machine-enforced (issue #107).

Owner: `{{owner}}` (see `.github/CODEOWNERS`).

## Public API

Code outside this module imports it **only** through the module barrel
`@/modules/{{module}}` (`src/modules/{{module}}/index.ts`). Deep imports fail
`no-module-internal-imports` in `make lint-deps`. Everything not re-exported there is
private.

The scaffold exports the repository contract types only. Add a symbol to the barrel
when — and only when — it genuinely has to cross the boundary.

## Layers

- `config/tokens.ts` — module DI symbols (`{{constantCase module}}_TOKENS`).
- `config/di.ts` — module composition root implementing `ModuleRegistrar`.
- `features/{{feature}}/index.tsx` — the feature entry component (the routed page).
- `features/{{feature}}/components/` — presentational components.
- `features/{{feature}}/hooks/` — UI logic; the only layer that drives repositories.
- `features/{{feature}}/repositories/` — data access, entered through its `index.ts`.
- `features/{{feature}}/stores/index.ts` — the one sanctioned DI seam for this feature.
- `features/{{feature}}/routes/index.ts` — the module-owned route contract.
- `features/{{feature}}/types/` — type-only files (issue #88).
- `features/{{feature}}/i18n/` — `en.json` and `uk.json`.

Allowed folder names come from `config/module-shape.json`, the single source both the
generator and `.dependency-cruiser.js` read. See
[the scaffolding guide](../../../docs/scaffolding.md).

## Finish the wiring

The generator writes everything it can create safely. Two hand-maintained,
order-sensitive spots are left to you, and `make new-module` / `make new-feature` print
the exact snippets:

1. `src/config/dependency-injection-config.ts` — import this module's registrar and add
   it to the `registrars` array, otherwise `config/di.ts` never registers anything.
2. `src/routes/registry.ts` — import `{{camelCase feature}}Routes` and append it to
   `routeModules`, otherwise the page is unreachable.

Do the route one first: `tests/e2e/modules/{{module}}/features/{{feature}}/{{feature}}.spec.ts`
ships live, because the suite bans skipped tests, so it fails until the page is reachable.

